## Why This Is Asked
Tests depth in deploying custom ops with SavedModel and zero-downtime canary rollouts, plus cross-arch building for CPU/GPU.

## Key Concepts
- TensorFlow custom ops and savedmodel integration
- Bazel/BUILD for CPU and GPU
- custom_op_library linking
- Signature definitions in TF Serving
- Canary deployments and traffic shifting with Istio

## Code Example
```cpp
// Minimal custom op skeleton
#include "tensorflow/core/framework/op.h"
#include "tensorflow/core/framework/op_kernel.h"

REGISTER_OP("CustomOp")
  .Input("in: float")
  .Output("out: float");

class CustomOpKernel : public OpKernel {
 public:
  explicit CustomOpKernel(OpKernelConstruction* ctx) : OpKernel(ctx) {}
  void Compute(OpKernelContext* ctx) override {
    // Implementation placeholder
  }
};

REGISTER_KERNEL_BUILDER(Name("CustomOp").Device(DEVICE_CPU), CustomOpKernel);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor correctness across CPU vs GPU builds?
- How would you handle versioned breaking changes to the op signature?

## Why This Is Asked
